    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After the medical entrance exam on May 3, a whistleblower in Sikar sent an email to the National Testing Agency, an institutional authority restoring order, with PDFs that matched 100% of the chemistry questions and part of biology, exposing a leak of exam materials. The governing body promptly escalated the matter to the CBI, a restorer of institutional control, leading to an enforcement action against disruptors. This swift response resulted in the containment of the institutional breach, with thirteen perpetrators of a systemic breach arrested and the NEET-UG 2026 exam cancelled to restore orderly process.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "result-1"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.88
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "A tip from an informant in the city of Sikar uncovered systemic rule-breaking involving paper setters and translators. The government agency, acting as an institutional authority, referred the matter to law enforcement, initiating an investigation. The subsequent arrests, including that of a public figure who had championed student justice, marked an enforcement action against those who threatened institutional integrity. The decision to cancel the entrance exam and schedule a re-examination for June 21 represents the restoration of an orderly process, moving to contain the scandal.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "The revelation of a leak of exam materials via a tipster's report forced the nation's testing agency to confront a breach of institutional control. The authority escalated the issue to the investigation agency, a bureau tasked with restoring order. The law enforcement action against a group of individuals, including a prominent educator, served to contain the disruption. The cancellation of the medical entrance exam, an event outcome, was a necessary measure to halt public life due to the unmanaged scandal, while the planned re-examination for June 21 signals a return to a structured timeline.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Ruler",
